@using ITMartin.Shared.UI.Kolibri
@inject KolibriAppInfo Info
@* The tab title when a page sets none: the app's name. Put it DIRECTLY in the layout, before @Body - NOT inside another component:
   Blazor renders level by level and the deepest <PageTitle> registers last and wins. Inside KolibriHeader it sat one level deeper
   than the page's own <PageTitle>, so every tab read the app name (found 2026-11-12 on elpriser.itmartin.dk/regning). App.razor must NOT have a fixed <title>: browsers show the FIRST <title>, so every page
   read the same name in the tab, on Google and in the visit numbers (2026-10-27, itmartin.dk/admin/tal). *@
<PageTitle>@(string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(Text) ? Info.Name : Text)</PageTitle>

@code {
    /// <summary>Fallback title instead of the app's name.</summary>
    [Parameter] public string? Text { get; set; }
}
